Description: Let a distro page read a switch of its own from plasma-welcomerc
 Distro.flag(key) reads the key of the [Distribution] group of
 plasma-welcomerc as KConfig reads it: the user's file, then each folder of
 XDG_CONFIG_DIRS; a key no file sets reads false. A page's `show` can then
 depend on the kind of machine: Sparky Stereo OS shows its touch page only where
 its hardware layer finds a touch screen of the computer's own, by a session
 script that puts a folder with its own plasma-welcomerc in front of
 XDG_CONFIG_DIRS. A page cannot wait for a command before it is shown
 (Main.qml reads `show` once, when it creates the page), and nothing public in
 org.kde.plasma.welcome reads configuration.
